                "entry_id": "1b8fbc78-5b2e-3eec-b715-4759ad3b4977",
                "word": "cryptolecte",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "930ed2d3-adfa-453a-b44b-0e99102933cb",
                        "entry_id": "1b8fbc78-5b2e-3eec-b715-4759ad3b4977",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "cryptolectes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e5babd9d-71cc-3d2d-99a3-31de5f9b9436",
                        "entry_id": "1b8fbc78-5b2e-3eec-b715-4759ad3b4977",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Idiome parlé et compris par uniquement certains membres d’une population dans le but de communiquer entre eux en restant inintelligible pour l’extérieur du groupe."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "eb28e375-5b98-40be-87e6-769d4f68dd1c",
                                "sense_id": "e5babd9d-71cc-3d2d-99a3-31de5f9b9436",
                                "text": "Le linguiste peut légitimement, semble-t-il, en conclure qu’il y a cryptoglosse, ou cryptolecte, pour être cohérent avec le choix terminologique effectué ci-dessus. Ce type de comportement peut n’être que le point d’aboutissement extrême de l’idéologie disglossique et du processus de standardisation, ou encore une indication que la communauté linguistique concernée ne se sent pas assez légitime face à un lecte pour s’autoriser à le légitimer (plausible en situation de francophonie hors de France)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cbfccec5-0c79-4af3-aa39-10df608ae5c1",
                                "sense_id": "e5babd9d-71cc-3d2d-99a3-31de5f9b9436",
                                "text": "Virer assassin, est-ce que j’avais le choix ? Huit ans que j’avais... aucune instruction... privé de langue... comment j’aurais pu me défendre ? Le Yéniche c’est quoi ? Un sociolecte... un cryptolecte, selon les plus généreux... C’est pas vraiment une arme face à qui pratique la langue d’Homère et celle des pères de l’Église."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9feeea74-beb6-402a-857a-7cc532fdd504",
                        "source_entry_id": "1b8fbc78-5b2e-3eec-b715-4759ad3b4977",
                        "source_sense_id": "e5babd9d-71cc-3d2d-99a3-31de5f9b9436",
                        "target_lang_word": "cryptolect",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cryptolect",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fa66d437-e8cc-3a59-829e-7430d0a77534",
                                        "entry_id": "ba0ce5fc-a3a9-34c9-90cb-5b1a95f16cf5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A secretive language form used by a subculture; an arcane cant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8d9a707-aca9-40df-9a9d-b246d15da14d",
                                                "sense_id": "fa66d437-e8cc-3a59-829e-7430d0a77534",
                                                "text": "Cockney rhyming slang developed originally from the cryptolects of London’s thieves and vagabonds."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d092b6c9-2f0f-4380-8f2b-646123340542",
                        "source_entry_id": "1b8fbc78-5b2e-3eec-b715-4759ad3b4977",
                        "source_sense_id": "e5babd9d-71cc-3d2d-99a3-31de5f9b9436",
                        "target_lang_word": "cant",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "75642a65-ff7a-34b1-a426-08935dc2d227",
                                        "entry_id": "7e47f204-2923-383c-ae8d-567ce5075819",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An argot, the jargon of a particular class or subgroup."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3bb87373-8dab-4088-be71-2cb8640c336b",
                                                "sense_id": "75642a65-ff7a-34b1-a426-08935dc2d227",
                                                "text": "He had the look of a prince, but the cant of a fishmonger."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a854634-5b80-48ab-8e6a-b9c354ba18ba",
                                                "sense_id": "75642a65-ff7a-34b1-a426-08935dc2d227",
                                                "text": "I am aware that the phrase free inquiry has become too much a cant phrase soiled by the handling of the ignorant and the reckless by those who fall into the mistake of supposing that religion has its root in the understanding and by those who can see just far enough to doubt and no further."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a26323d-26ff-3f11-ad7d-dcc06b9ee17b",
                                        "entry_id": "7e47f204-2923-383c-ae8d-567ce5075819",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A private or secret language used by a religious sect, gang, or other group."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ce3e22e7-de7f-3e5a-94b8-e170f022b499",
                                        "entry_id": "7e47f204-2923-383c-ae8d-567ce5075819",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A language spoken by some Irish Travellers; Shelta."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8f986a89-c4dc-3adb-a7fd-ed3357fcc57c",
                                        "entry_id": "7e47f204-2923-383c-ae8d-567ce5075819",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Empty, hypocritical talk."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8ad7845-9ea8-4b33-ab0a-58e3976a9ebd",
                                                "sense_id": "8f986a89-c4dc-3adb-a7fd-ed3357fcc57c",
                                                "text": "Of all the cants which are canted in this canting world,—though the cant of hypocrites may be the worſt,—the cant of criticiſm is the moſt tormenting!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2fc0f007-3e9d-4d14-aece-14af2c67f22b",
                                                "sense_id": "8f986a89-c4dc-3adb-a7fd-ed3357fcc57c",
                                                "text": "He is too well grounded for all your philoſophical Cant to hurt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73aa2e9a-8c73-4e88-b73a-d6c30f613ddc",
                                                "sense_id": "8f986a89-c4dc-3adb-a7fd-ed3357fcc57c",
                                                "text": "... he knew very well that if they thought him clever they were being taken in, but it pleased him to have been able to take them in, and he tried to do so still further; he was therefore a good deal on the look-out for cants that he could catch and apply in season, and might have done himself some mischief thus if he had not been ready to throw over any cant as soon as he had come across another more nearly to his fancy ..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "018d3027-74ef-4e11-b444-c71d8c924fc7",
                                                "sense_id": "8f986a89-c4dc-3adb-a7fd-ed3357fcc57c",
                                                "text": "The German population as a whole had been fed 12 years of Nazi propaganda, including demonizing and dehumanizing cant about homosexual men and women."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cd9b697d-89de-36a6-b16b-0533664f9236",
                                        "entry_id": "7e47f204-2923-383c-ae8d-567ce5075819",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Whining speech, such as that used by beggars."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2d9b22bd-2aef-3cc7-bc10-52f0267b64bb",
                                        "entry_id": "7e47f204-2923-383c-ae8d-567ce5075819",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A blazon of a coat of arms that makes a pun upon the name (or, less often, some attribute or function) of the bearer, canting arms."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3112d827-1493-3a47-bb06-57bc420ad4cd",
                                        "entry_id": "7e47f204-2923-383c-ae8d-567ce5075819",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A call for bidders at a public fair; an auction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "614fdf01-910b-43c1-ab18-f2064f44d11a",
                                                "sense_id": "3112d827-1493-3a47-bb06-57bc420ad4cd",
                                                "text": "[…]but numbers of these tenants or their descendants are now offering to sell their leases by cant,"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "cant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c8760692-f730-352e-a8e2-bf17b9d90673",
                                        "entry_id": "07e6f5b1-12bf-3fcd-98ab-26e6af2c86c9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To speak with the jargon of a class or subgroup."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "56f88a46-41c5-448f-8b8e-78450f764cc1",
                                                "sense_id": "c8760692-f730-352e-a8e2-bf17b9d90673",
                                                "text": "The Doctor here, I will proceed with the learned. / VVhen he diſcourſeth of diſſection, / Or any point of Anatomy: that hee tells you, / Of Vena caua, and of vena porta, / The Meſeraicks, and the Meſenterium. / VVhat does he elſe but cant? […] / Does he not cant? VVho here does vnderſtand him?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "906924a2-c7ab-42a7-841f-41798789788a",
                                                "sense_id": "c8760692-f730-352e-a8e2-bf17b9d90673",
                                                "text": "[…]that uncouth affected garb of speech, or canting language rather, if I may so call it"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "320acbc2-fd63-3fba-9fa4-ea6c94775e1c",
                                        "entry_id": "07e6f5b1-12bf-3fcd-98ab-26e6af2c86c9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To speak in set phrases."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dd4f1716-cb66-383d-9de9-a1daa3023c87",
                                        "entry_id": "07e6f5b1-12bf-3fcd-98ab-26e6af2c86c9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To talk, beg, or preach in a singsong or whining fashion, especially in a false or empty manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e1c3161-a752-4419-97e6-6418354898f4",
                                                "sense_id": "dd4f1716-cb66-383d-9de9-a1daa3023c87",
                                                "text": "[I]f he proue not yet / The cunningſt, ranckeſt Rogue that euer Canted, / Ile neuer ſee man againe, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4bdd05d3-cb84-4f61-b8a3-33bc35c1e5af",
                                                "sense_id": "dd4f1716-cb66-383d-9de9-a1daa3023c87",
                                                "text": "[S]he was one of your ſoft ſpoken, canting, whining hypocrites, who with a truly jeſuitical art, could wreſt evil out of the moſt inoffenſive thought, word, look or action; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "93ae3a6d-5130-3821-ac86-163f36877b0a",
                                        "entry_id": "07e6f5b1-12bf-3fcd-98ab-26e6af2c86c9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a blazon, to make a pun that references the bearer of a coat of arms."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1fe0af69-47f3-36d1-855b-155e1bba6b1d",
                                        "entry_id": "07e6f5b1-12bf-3fcd-98ab-26e6af2c86c9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To sell by auction, or bid at an auction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "359f44a5-a0be-43d7-b2dd-ac9fa988f461",
                                                "sense_id": "1fe0af69-47f3-36d1-855b-155e1bba6b1d",
                                                "text": "[…]labouring with all their might for preventing the bishops from letting their revenues at a moderate half value[…] at the very instant, when they were every where canting their own land upon short leases, and sacrificing their oldest tenants for a penny an acre advance."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "cant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b7995621-d644-374a-bb56-b3d2f32bfe79",
                                        "entry_id": "d2cb4cb8-7b5d-35b9-9351-32c3b9c12a2e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Side, edge, corner, niche."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
